            <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-waterfowl_beaks>,
            <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-why_wings> ;
        mlt:nCladeStudiesLocked 15 ;
        mlt:nTotalHypothesesLocked 77 ;
        mlt:scoutManifestSha256 "c79563c6bcab8c03f53375863abb573df47446b8b24be727f398b61a97b80790" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-antillean_flowers> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "seed plants: Antillean Gesneriaceae angiosperm corollas (Joly et al. 2018 Evolution / Zenodo 5011744: 296 corollas across 48 species on *BEAST tree; 32 2D floral landmarks across hummingbird, bat, and generalist pollination syndromes)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "antillean_flowers" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "05fd7c07e88a9c4bcadbf955ab584d9ee1f01da36a592737fdcf3030e99064c2" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"FP1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Angiosperm corolla tubes are ultra-Thompsonian: across the 48 Gesneriaceae species (32 2D landmarks), the 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture > 80% of between-species Procrustes variance.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"FP2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `BestTree.tre` is non-zero: Pagel's lambda > 0.5 (best model != White Noise) in Thompson-7 space.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"FP3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `BestTree.tre` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.90, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.01).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"FP4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Developmental/intraspecific channelling: within-species floral variation (pooled across the 296 corollas) aligns strongly with between-species floral divergence inside the Thompson-7 subspace (|cos theta|_T7 > 0.70 and |cos theta|_T7 > |cos theta|_res).\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-australian_frogs> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "amphibians: Continental radiation of Australian Anura (Sherratt et al. 2017 Evol Biol / Zenodo 5008593: 166 frog species on time-calibrated phylogeny; 55 2D larval tadpole body/tail landmarks + 21 adult postcranial/cranial traits)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "australian_frogs" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "5a6f11e8a8bf8eea1f8ec98921dcd818718e3ab5082d504324acb15dcf2fa993" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"AF1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Across the 166 Australian frog species (55 2D landmarks), the 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture > 70% of between-species Procrustes variance (exceeding marine reef fishes at 57.9%).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"AF2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on the 166-species anuran tree is non-zero: Pagel's lambda > 0.5 (best model != White Noise) in both Thompson-7 and full PCA-95% spaces.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"AF3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.85, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 1e-6) across the 166 species.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"AF4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures > 70% of the full-space phylogenetic prediction gain relative to consensus.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-bee_wings> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: bee (Anthophila) forewings across 10 families, with apoid-wasp outgroups and two Eocene fossil tribes" ;
        mlt:cladeId "bee_wings" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "c80c47f0c0b9cbf68df9e9482c45efd07662a3a3fca8ebb53aa1c2de16c46736" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 9 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"B1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.65, \"statement\": \"The 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture LESS than 58% (the fish value) of between-unit forewing variance, as in Vespinae (39%).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"A fitted 7-D PCA captures > 85% of between-unit variance (wing shape differences are low-dimensional even across families).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal is detectable: AICc selects a non-white-noise process in the full shape space AND Pagel's lambda fitted in that space exceeds 0.5.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B4\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.65, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-unit-out full-space phylogenetic prediction beats the grand consensus: median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.8, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.05.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Full-space prediction improves on copying the nearest unit's mean wing by less than 10% (ratio > 0.9), as in fish and hornets.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B6\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"The residual after the 7 Thompson modes concentrates in interior landmarks: mean unexplained fraction of the middle landmarks exceeds that of both ends of the long axis (replicating Vespinae).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B7\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"Horizon effect: units whose nearest other unit is > 60 Myr away have median full-space LOO error at least 1.5x that of units with a relative within 30 Myr.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B8\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Fossil time-slice test: the predicted stem-Apini lineage state at 45 Ma is closer (Procrustes RMS) to the observed mean wing of each Eocene corbiculate tribe (Electrapini, Melikertini) than the extant grand consensus is, for BOTH tribes.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"B9\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Conditional on B4: the 7 Thompson modes capture less than 55.5% (fish) of the full-space prediction gain over the consensus.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-camponotus_ants> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: Camponotus carpenter ants (4 structures: 82-LM frontal head, 61-LM lateral head, 52-LM pronotum, 46-LM mesosoma; 634 specimens across minor/media/major castes and 43 species)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "camponotus_ants" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "af0a81dd7dad89e317ea5f7f9ded598de7249ec4fbc4a5a0a8ed2fba151a9798" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 8 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"A1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Within-species minor ('w') -> major ('s') caste vectors are MORE Thompsonian than between-species species-mean divergence: pooled across the 42 dimorphic species on the 82-landmark frontal head, the 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture a larger share of within-species minor->major caste variance than of between-species species-mean variance (and > 50% of caste variance).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Across all 4 structures (frontal head 82 LM, lateral head 61 LM, pronotum 52 LM, mesosoma 46 LM), within-species minor->major caste vectors have a higher Thompson-7 variance share than between-species divergence in at least 3 of the 4 structures.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"Between-species frontal-head shape (82 LMs, 41 tree species) is MORE Thompsonian than insect wing venation: Thompson-7 captures > 0.422 (the bee-wing benchmark) of between-species variance in species-mean frontal heads.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `tree_CAM.tre`: Pagel's lambda (or BM/OU/EB over White Noise by AICc) is non-zero (lambda > 0.3, best model != White Noise) in Thompson-7 scores across all 4 structures.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.65, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction beats the consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.95, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.05) in at least 2 of the 4 structures.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A6\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures at least 50% of the full-space leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction gain (relative to consensus) on the frontal head (82 LMs), matching or exceeding fish bodies (55.5%).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A7\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Developmental channelling (G_caste vs R_species): the principal axis of within-species minor->major caste divergence aligns more strongly with the principal axis of between-species macroevolutionary divergence inside the 7-D Thompson subspace than in the orthogonal non-Thompson modular residual subspace (|cos theta|_T7 > |cos theta|_res) across at least 3 of the 4 structures.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"A8\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Where the global grid fails on the 82-LM frontal head: between-species unexplained residual fraction after Thompson-7 is HIGHER on interior/anterior sensory-oral landmarks (mandibles, clypeus, frontal carinae, eyes: landmarks closest to the centroid/anterior oral pole) than on the outer lateral/occipital head-capsule contour.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-characiformes_burns_gm> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "ray-finned fishes: Characiformes radiation (Burns & Sidlauskas 2019 Evolution: 1,625 specimens, 128 species on trees_final.nexus; 24-LM body shape)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "characiformes_burns_gm" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "d1a07c13c8e3b58a7aa13b1e78b23ee0d7a59b1d5ec13cca3f5beb7a4a2b4acc" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"CB1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Across the 128 Characiformes tree species (24 2D landmarks), Thompson-7 captures > 55% of between-species Procrustes variance.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CB2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `trees_final.nexus` is strong: Pagel's lambda > 0.7 (best model != White Noise) in both Thompson-7 and full PCA-95% spaces.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CB3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `trees_final.nexus` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.75, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 1e-8).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CB4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Head/eye/opercle interior landmarks have a higher unexplained residual fraction after Thompson-7 than the outer dorsal/ventral/caudal body contour landmarks.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-cichlids_ronco_gm> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "ray-finned fishes: Lake Tanganyika cichlid radiation (Ronco et al. 2021 Nature: 2,197 specimens, ~235 species on 05_BEAST_RAxML.tre; 21-LM body shape vs 27-LM lower pharyngeal jaw)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "cichlids_ronco_gm" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "c07c8c49a82ba65051f21d741b6fff2bb3769d890cf4e2fa283171200ddd4ed7" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"CR1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Across the ~235 Tanganyika cichlid species on `05_BEAST_RAxML.tre`, Thompson-7 captures > 55% of between-species Procrustes variance on the 21-LM body shape (matching the 57.9% marine reef-fish benchmark).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CR2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.95, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `05_BEAST_RAxML.tre` strongly beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.65, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 1e-10) on 21-LM body shape.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CR3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures > 60% of the full-space phylogenetic prediction gain on 21-LM body shape AND beats the consensus on its own (Wilcoxon p < 1e-10).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"CR4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Internal trophic jaw vs external body: the 27-LM Lower Pharyngeal Jaw (2D dorsal XY projection) is also strongly predicted by phylogeny (LOO ratio vs consensus < 0.75, Wilcoxon p < 1e-10) and has > 50% Thompson-7 variance share.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-drosophilidae_wings> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: Drosophilidae wings (Houle et al. 2017 Nature: 117 species, 21,138 species wings, 17,323 G-matrix wings, 12,075 M-matrix wings; 12 landmarks)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "drosophilidae_wings" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "dbd69f7224faae443f41c233f073bd00096f213348b98d0950c4c8c6ce83ef5b" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 5 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"DW1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Across the 117 drosophilid species means (12 2D landmarks), the 7 a-priori Thompson coordinate modes capture > 50% of between-species Procrustes variance (exceeding the 38.8% hornet and 42.2% bee forewing benchmarks).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"DW2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Interior crossvein landmarks (the 4 middle landmarks along the proximal-distal axis) have a higher unexplained residual fraction after Thompson-7 than the 8 proximal/apical margin landmarks.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"DW3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on the 88-species OpenTree topology: best multivariate evolutionary model in full PCA-95% space is NOT White Noise (Pagel's lambda > 0.3).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"DW4\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction in full shape space beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.95, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.01).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"DW5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Mutational-macroevolutionary alignment (Houle M vs D): in the 20-PC space of `AllAlignedNature.csv`, the leading axis of spontaneous mutational variance (M, n=12,075) and standing genetic variance (Gw, n=17,323) both align strongly with between-species macroevolutionary divergence (D, n=21,138), with |cos theta| > 0.50.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-galeommatoidea_bivalves> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "molluscs: Galeommatoidea marine bivalve shells (Goto et al. 2016 Evolution: 302 specimens, ~100 species on final_BEAST.tre; 46 shell-outline landmarks)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "galeommatoidea_bivalves" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "805386b0e5a858e77eae8c42819d5cf16e43d51883a8afad0fa87af47d88c828" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"GB1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Bivalve shells are ultra-Thompsonian: across the ~100 Galeommatoidea species means (46 2D landmarks), the 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture > 85% of between-species Procrustes variance (exceeding fish bodies, insect wings, and vertebrate skulls).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"GB2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `final_BEAST.tre` is non-zero: Pagel's lambda > 0.5 (best model != White Noise) in both Thompson-7 and full PCA-95% spaces.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"GB3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `final_BEAST.tre` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.85, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.001).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"GB4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures > 85% of the full-space phylogenetic prediction gain relative to consensus.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-leporidae_skulls> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "mammals: Lagomorpha / Leporidae crania (Sherratt & Kraatz 2023 Evolution: 317 specimens, 23 species on Matthee_Tree.nex; 74 cranial landmarks)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "leporidae_skulls" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "d228f85c1bbd4cd8c9d3c1f06fa6124bd2a61e9c466b8296773c5c925f0abe47" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 3 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"LS1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Across the 23 lagomorph species means on the 74-LM lateral cranial profile, Thompson-7 captures > 55% of between-species Procrustes variance.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"LS2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `Matthee_Tree.nex` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.95, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.05) on the cranial profile.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"LS3\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Within-species intraspecific cranial variation (pooled across the 317 specimens) has a higher or comparable Thompson-7 variance share (> 45%) and aligns significantly with interspecific divergence inside the Thompson-7 subspace (|cos theta|_T7 > 0.5).\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-morpho_butterflies> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: Morpho butterflies (Chazot et al. 2021 J Evol Biol: 911 specimens, 30 species on Morpho_MCC_tree.tre; forewing 22 LMs & hindwing 18 LMs)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "morpho_butterflies" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "637c8a2a2bef27576a8ad7e29358d677cacf047b7b213a002c3346bb3f936654" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"MB1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Across the 30 Morpho species means, Thompson-7 captures > 45% of between-species Procrustes variance on both forewings (22 LMs) and hindwings (18 LMs).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"MB2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `Morpho_MCC_tree.tre`: Pagel's lambda > 0.5 (best model != White Noise) in both forewing and hindwing shape spaces.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"MB3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `Morpho_MCC_tree.tre` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.90, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.01) on forewing shape.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"MB4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Sexual dimorphism vs interspecific divergence: within-species male -> female wing shape vectors have a higher Thompson-7 variance share than between-species divergence on the forewing.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-pheidole_ants> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: Pheidole big-headed ants (Friedman et al. 2019: 651 minor heads, 502 major heads [23 LMs], minor & major mesosomas [10 LMs] across ~200 species on Pheidole_Tree.phy)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "pheidole_ants" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "50090939d34cb5f4deefc838b1a6fecfa0d31eaf555d8a2b5bc82444c838d0a2" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 5 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"PH1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Between-species 23-LM head shape in both minor workers and major soldiers is strongly Thompsonian: Thompson-7 captures > 60% of interspecific Procrustes variance across the ~200 Pheidole species.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"PH2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Within-species minor -> major soldier caste transformation vectors on the 23-LM head are well-captured by Thompson's 7 global coordinate modes (> 55% of pooled caste-shift variance).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"PH3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Developmental channelling (G_caste vs R_species): the principal axis of within-species minor->major caste divergence aligns more strongly with the principal axis of between-species macroevolutionary divergence inside the 7-D Thompson subspace than in the orthogonal non-Thompson residual subspace (|cos theta|_T7 > |cos theta|_res) on the 23-LM head.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"PH4\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `Pheidole_Tree.phy` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.95, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.01) for minor head shape.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"PH5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Interior sensory/oral landmarks (eyes, antennal insertions, clypeus: the 8 landmarks closest to the anterior/interior centroid) have a higher unexplained residual fraction after Thompson-7 than the 15 outer head-capsule contour landmarks.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-varanus_lizards> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "squamate reptiles: Indo-Australasian Varanus monitor lizards (Brennan et al. 2021 Syst Biol / Zenodo 5655818: 1,091 dorsal + 1,098 lateral crania across 80 taxa on calibrated Tree.tre; 33 dorsal LMs & 10 lateral LMs)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "varanus_lizards" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "ef9803547c4e51fb7358859e550ba1c3c270a4f8904c175004381324ef017216" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"VL1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Across the ~80 Varanus taxa, Thompson-7 captures > 55% of between-species Procrustes variance on both dorsal (33 LMs) and lateral (10 LMs) head views.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"VL2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on `Tree.tre` is strong: Pagel's lambda > 0.7 (best model != White Noise) in Thompson-7 space for both dorsal and lateral head views.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"VL3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction on `Tree.tre` beats the grand consensus (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.85, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 1e-5) on dorsal head shape.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"VL4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"Within-species intraspecific/ontogenetic cranial variation aligns more strongly with between-species divergence inside the 7-D Thompson subspace than in the orthogonal modular residual subspace (|cos theta|_T7 > |cos theta|_res) on the 33-LM dorsal head.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-vespinae_wings> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "insects: Vespinae hornet and yellowjacket forewings" ;
        mlt:cladeId "vespinae_wings" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "a4491b13be39863e6943d01d93a5fe25a9462cfbd2b5b74352b1970a4a5d128e" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 7 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"W1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"The 7 generic Thompson modes capture a LARGER share of between-species wing-shape variance in Vespinae than in fish bodies: > 0.58 (species means after GPA).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures a LARGER share of the full-space leave-one-species-out prediction gain (relative to the consensus) than in fish: > 0.555.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.8, \"statement\": \"Full-space phylogenetic prediction beats the consensus in leave-one-species-out (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.8, paired Wilcoxon p < 0.05 given n = 30).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Full-space prediction improves on copying the nearest relative's mean wing by less than 10% (ratio > 0.9), as in fish.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.65, \"statement\": \"Pagel's lambda fitted on the Thompson-7 scores exceeds 0.7 (strong phylogenetic signal in the global deformation modes).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W6\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.75, \"statement\": \"A data-driven 7-D PCA basis still beats the a-priori Thompson-7 basis in representation (variance captured) AND in prediction, as in fish.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"W7\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.55, \"statement\": \"Representation of species differences by Thompson-7 is not uniform across the wing: the residual after the 7 global modes concentrates in the distal/apical landmarks (marginal cell and apex), i.e. the Thompsonian description fails locally where the venation is most variable.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-waterfowl_beaks> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "birds: Anseriformes waterfowl beaks (Olsen 2017 Evolution: 51 species on Burleigh_2015.tre; 2D dorsal/lateral upper-bill culmen & tomium contour landmarks)" ;
        mlt:cladeId "waterfowl_beaks" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "c75576f2f59e7701771c5f01997ff16ef820d4570c550495f0a272873f9b63e6" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 4 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"WB1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Bird beak profiles are exceptionally Thompsonian: across the 51 waterfowl species, the 7 a-priori Thompson modes capture > 80% of between-species Procrustes variance on the 2D lateral beak outline (exceeding fish bodies at 57.9%).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"WB2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.9, \"statement\": \"Phylogenetic signal on the 51-species waterfowl tree is strong: Pagel's lambda > 0.7 (best model != White Noise) in both Thompson-7 and full PCA-95% spaces.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"WB3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.95, \"statement\": \"Leave-one-species-out phylogenetic prediction beats the grand consensus by a wide margin (median Procrustes RMS ratio < 0.75, paired one-sided Wilcoxon p < 0.001).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"WB4\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.85, \"statement\": \"Thompson-7 captures > 80% of the full-space phylogenetic prediction gain relative to consensus.\"}" .

    <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/portfolio/multiclade-preregistration-manifest-2026-10-23-why_wings> a mlt:CladeHypothesisRegistration ;
        rdfs:label "why_wings" ;
        mlt:cladeId "why_wings" ;
        mlt:hypothesisFileSha256 "7a6c1f5a8f09672dbe0129e4f994d49a30aef3035055b9c0185ad8312a2e3b42" ;
        mlt:nHypotheses 8 ;
        mlt:registeredHypothesis "{\"id\": \"C1\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"The per-landmark fraction of among-unit variance NOT captured by T7 is NOT predicted by per-landmark within-unit variance (Spearman rho <= 0.5 or p >= 0.05). I.e. the residual pattern is not a digitising artefact.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C2\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.7, \"statement\": \"Among-unit divergence is aligned with the within-unit covariance structure: the angle between d_max (leading eigenvector of the among-unit covariance) and p_max (leading eigenvector of pooled within-unit P) is below the 5th percentile of random-direction angles in the tangent space, AND the first 3 within-unit PCs carry more than twice the random-expectation share of among-unit variance.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C3\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.55, \"statement\": \"Brownian motion on the group's tree with rate matrix proportional to P (plus sampling error P/n_u at the tips) reproduces the observed T7 variance share: the observed share lies inside the central 90% of 2000 simulated shares.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C4\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.5, \"statement\": \"The same simulation reproduces the observed residual location: the observed ratio (mean unexplained fraction at the 10 long-axis-end landmarks) / (mean unexplained fraction at the middle landmarks) lies inside the central 90% of simulated ratios.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C5\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.4, \"statement\": \"The within-unit covariance P is itself less Thompsonian than among-unit divergence: the T7 share of trace(P) is at least 10 percentage points below the T7 share of among-unit variance.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C6\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"Evolutionary allometry is substantial: log centroid size (pixel, single-lab imaging; species order validated against known body sizes before registration) explains >= 15% of among-species shape variance (multivariate regression, permutation p < 0.05).\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C7\", \"primary\": true, \"p\": 0.6, \"statement\": \"The allometric direction is more Thompsonian than divergence in general: the T7 share of the size-regression vector exceeds the overall among-species T7 share (0.388) by at least 10 percentage points.\"}",
            "{\"id\": \"C8\", \"primary\": false, \"p\": 0.55, \"statement\": \"Removing allometry removes the Thompsonian signal: the T7 share of size-corrected residual shape is at least 5 percentage points below the uncorrected share.\"}" .
}

